{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgdQzXEvHMui5K8vVA1j4", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**The Last Keeper**\n\nFor forty years, Mara climbed the iron stairs of Gull Point every dusk to light the lamp. The ships had long since gone GPS, and the government had sent letters about automation. She kept climbing anyway.\n\nThen the storm came in October, black and sudden, and the grid failed at 4 p.m. The radar screens died. The harbor went dark.\n\nMara reached the lantern room with frost in her lungs and lit the old wick by hand. The beam swept out over the water, slow and steady, the way it always had.\n\nOut past the reef, a fishing boat wavered, its captain staring at nothing. Then he saw the light, turned his bow toward it, and followed it home.\n\nThe next morning, the town gathered on the rocks. They found Mara asleep in the lantern room, her hand still on the brass rail, the wick glowing faintly beside her.\n\nA young reporter asked why she had bothered, when machines could do the job.\n\nMara smiled and wiped the salt from the glass.\n\n\"Machines don't stay awake for strangers,\" she said."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4003, "cache_read_input_tokens": 13919, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4003}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "steer-session-1", "uuid": "1162e879-9cbc-4274-9201-72d95709994b", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T03:45:56.867Z", "request_id": "req_011CgdQzX4kZFYg1GXnkj4ch"}
